  "checksDetail": [
    "Both solids start at ambient during ordinary cold initialization, lag the gas bath, preserve heat through cutoff, and cool after shutdown.",
    "Repeated property reads, native hold, suspended integration, zero-time RunIC, repeated InitRunning, and positive-dt trim retain both solid states.",
    "State properties are independent RW; temperature and initialized observations reject writes. Restoring core does not initialize liner.",
    "Native reset/reload clears both states; exact restoration cancels warm seeding, and each next accepted step stays within the declared continuity bound.",
    "Application snapshot/free/departure/arrival relocation preserves both temperatures exactly before advancing.",
    "Static stopped-hot runway relocation retains both temperatures and remains stopped with zero fuel over 120 accepted steps.",
    "Dry99 heats both solids from idle; afterburner heats downstream gas/liner while core sees its unchanged upstream EGT bath. Both hot/cold histories return to the same dry99 equilibria.",
    "Every accepted powered-lift step keeps augmentation off, including conversion transient, while dry gas and both solids remain heated."
  ],
  "tolerances": {
    "exactStateKelvin": 1e-08,
    "nextStepFraction": 0.02,
    "dryEquilibriumAgreementKelvin": 1,
